The CEDFrequencyMerger and CEDTemporalMapper definitions and initialization
are retained from Mizar runtime/stage1/models/ced.py. The CED encoder model
code and weights are separate remote assets and retain their own terms.

This isolated route reuses CED/projector construction, raw-byte staging,
adaptive gradient clipping and complete-state checkpoints from the local
Mizar training adaptations. It inherits the original official 454 states,
then adds two independent sigmoid residual gates and two repeat biases.
It uses the complete filtered S3 pool, center20 online audio, eight-GPU
microbatch-four with four-step gradient accumulation, and grouped LRs.
Reference source file identities are recorded in parent_sources.json.
